  transform:
    description: |
      Wave-shift rows relative to the bottom row of the object bbox.
      Bottom row (distance 0) is fixed. Even-distance rows are fixed.
      Odd-distance rows shift by 1px: d=1 left, d=3 right, d=5 left, d=7 right, ...
    shifted_rows_must_not_collide: true (after clearing old positions, new positions must be bg)

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (input is the constrained object; transform is deterministic)
  steps:
    - Pick grid dims (13-15 x 14-15), fg color, bg=0
    - Choose n_hbars (2-4) and n_vbar_groups (2-3)
    - Choose uniform cell_width (1-4) and cell_height (2-11)
    - Compute object size from bars+cells; ensure object fits with >=2 margin on each side
    - Place the lattice on a bg grid at a random position respecting margins
    - Verify the lattice forms one 4-connected component
    - Output is produced by applying the wave shift; no generation needed
  constraints:
    - left and right margins >= 2 guarantees shifted output stays in bounds
    - Keep object_height 7-13 and object_width 5-9 by constraining bar/cell counts
